{
  "$comment": [
    "Tier-2 DB-state fixture spec for the `chats` repo (Phase-2). Both the v4",
    "oracle (chats-tier2.ts) and the Rust port read this file.",
    "",
    "OPEN-JSON KEY-ORDER (seam #5 \u2014 now CLOSED): `state` and `sillyTavernMetadata`",
    "are both JsonSchema = z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()) \u2014 arbitrary JSON whose",
    "keys pass through verbatim. v4 serializes via JSON.stringify (INSERTION order);",
    "the Rust port stores them as raw serde_json::Value serialized under the",
    "`preserve_order` feature (enabled workspace-wide), which ALSO preserves",
    "insertion order. The FIRST create op supplies both columns MULTI-KEY in",
    "DELIBERATELY NON-SORTED order:",
    "  - state:              { zeta, alpha, mode }   (sorted: alpha, mode, zeta)",
    "  - sillyTavernMetadata: { yankee, bravo, charlie } (sorted: bravo, charlie, yankee)",
    "so sorted order differs from insertion order \u2014 the green diff PROVES the port",
    "emits insertion order, not sorted keys. (Before preserve_order these would have",
    "diverged; the old single-key `state` and absent sillyTavernMetadata could not",
    "tell.)",
    "P4.D226 (v4 `4d370a90f`, #75): the Concierge state ops — a create carrying the trio and three that do not (NULL, never a `moderated` literal); `setConciergeMode` unconditional, NULL (c4) and a literal (c3) counted as Moderated, a miss (c2 is locked), a literal match, matched-but-unchanged still written, a non-moderated expected that misses, a missing chat; a whole-row update that leaves the trio alone (v4 `patchOnlyFields`); `setDangerClassification` (telemetry only, the verdict never stored, a missing chat)."
  ],
